Alembic migrations for FinSight.

PostgreSQL is authoritative for all application state, so every schema change
arrives here as a reviewed, reversible revision.

Run from the repository root with the project virtual environment activated:

    alembic upgrade head          apply every pending revision
    alembic current               show the revision the database is on
    alembic downgrade -1          reverse the most recent revision

The database URL is not configured in alembic.ini. env.py builds it from
application settings so the password stays in .env alone. Offline mode
(--sql) is refused for the same reason.

Readiness reports the schema as current only when the database's revision
matches the head of this directory, which is why this directory must ship with
any image that serves the readiness endpoint.
